\chapter{Test organization and reproducible reports}
\label{ch:70}
\index{Test organization and reproducible reports}

CTest orchestrates compiler, runtime, standard-library, SDK and backend profiles when built with testing enabled. Python drivers exercise actual executables, while C and C++ tests can interrogate internal APIs or forge bad intermediate structures. Optional facilities may have skips or separate providers. Document which tests ran, which skipped, and how configurations differ before comparing totals.

\section{Build a minimal regression matrix}
For a language feature, create a positive source example, a negative type case, an execution oracle and, when a checked representation is exposed, an invalid-IR fixture. Test generated and fallback scanners where tokenization is relevant. Cover an optional backend separately with its own target and runtime. Include a relocation test for packaging changes and a sanitizer configuration for lifetimes. Record failures from untouched kernel-inventory checks as their own results. Avoid aggregating past results over incompatible trees or provider revisions as if they were one green run.

